%%{init: {'theme':'base', 'themeVariables': { 'primaryColor':'#1168bd','primaryTextColor':'#0B1930','primaryBorderColor':'#0a4d8c','lineColor':'#1a8fff','secondaryColor':'#087b7b','tertiaryColor':'#052E56','noteBkgColor':'#fef3c7','noteTextColor':'#0B1930','noteBorderColor':'#f59e0b'}}}%%

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    %% ============================================================================
    %% PARTICIPANTS
    %% ============================================================================

    actor User as 🎯 SE User
    participant FE as 📱 SE Frontend<br/>(React/Angular)
    participant BE as ⚙️ SE Backend<br/>(Spring Boot)
    participant CE as 🖥️ Calculation Engine<br/>(Spring Boot)
    participant DB as 🗄️ Source Database<br/>(PostgreSQL)
    participant SEDB as 🗃️ SE Database<br/>(PostgreSQL / TimescaleDB)

    %% ============================================================================
    %% PHASE 1 — USER TRIGGERS REQUEST  (REST/JSON, small control payload ~1 KB)
    %% ============================================================================

    rect rgb(219, 234, 254)
        Note over User,BE: 🌐 PHASE 1 — Initiate Request · REST / JSON · ~1 KB
        User->>+FE: 1️⃣ Click "Run Smeagol"
        FE->>+BE: 2️⃣ POST /api/smeagols<br/>REST / JSON · { system_id, params }<br/>Payload ~1 KB
        Note right of FE: ✅ REST/JSON optimal here.<br/>Tiny control message under 5 MB.<br/>Zero serialization overhead.
    end

    %% ============================================================================
    %% PHASE 2 — SE BACKEND → CALCULATION ENGINE  (gRPC, system_id only ~100 B)
    %% ============================================================================

    rect rgb(250, 232, 255)
        Note over BE,CE: ⚡ PHASE 2 — Forward system_id · gRPC / Protobuf · ~100 B
        BE->>+CE: 3️⃣ gRPC: TriggerCalculation(system_id)<br/>Protobuf message · ~100 B
        Note right of BE: ✅ gRPC chosen because:<br/>• HTTP/2 multiplexing<br/>• Protobuf ~10x smaller than JSON<br/>• Typed .proto contract<br/>• Native server-streaming for Phase 4
    end

    %% ============================================================================
    %% PHASE 3 — CALCULATION ENGINE → SOURCE DB  (JDBC streaming cursor)
    %% ============================================================================

    rect rgb(255, 247, 205)
        Note over CE,DB: 🗃️ PHASE 3 — Bulk DB Read · JDBC Streaming Cursor · 1M rows x 50 cols
        CE->>+DB: 4️⃣ JDBC streaming query<br/>SELECT * FROM source_table WHERE system_id = ?<br/>FETCH SIZE 5000 rows/batch
        Note right of CE: ✅ JDBC server-side cursor:<br/>• Rows fetched in 5K batches<br/>• Never loads full payload into heap<br/>• DB holds cursor between fetches<br/>• ~120-150 MB raw JSON-equivalent
        DB-->>-CE: 5️⃣ Row stream: 1 000 000 rows x 50 cols<br/>(JDBC ResultSet — server-side cursor)
        Note right of DB: 📦 Size estimates for 1M rows x 50 cols:<br/>JSON    ~120-150 MB  text, verbose<br/>XML     ~250-300 MB  2x JSON overhead<br/>Avro     ~15-25 MB  row binary, compressed<br/>Parquet   ~8-15 MB  columnar, best ratio
    end

    %% ============================================================================
    %% PHASE 4 — CALCULATION ENGINE → SE BACKEND  (gRPC server-streaming)
    %% ============================================================================

    rect rgb(250, 232, 255)
        Note over BE,CE: 🚀 PHASE 4 — Stream Results · gRPC Server-Streaming · Protobuf chunks
        CE-->>BE: 6️⃣ gRPC Server-Streaming RPC<br/>stream CalculationResponse repeated Row rows<br/>5000 rows/chunk · ~75 KB/chunk · 200 chunks total<br/>Wire size ~15-25 MB compressed Protobuf
        Note right of CE: ✅ gRPC server-streaming chosen:<br/>• CE pushes 200 chunks as rows arrive from DB<br/>• BE persists each chunk immediately on receipt<br/>• Zero full-payload buffering on either side<br/>• HTTP/2 flow control = natural back-pressure<br/>• Schema enforced by shared .proto contract
        activate BE
        Note over CE,BE: 🔄 Pipeline: each chunk persisted<br/>before the next chunk arrives
    end

    %% ============================================================================
    %% PHASE 5 — SE BACKEND → SE DATABASE  (JDBC batch insert, 5K rows/batch)
    %% ============================================================================

    rect rgb(204, 251, 241)
        Note over BE,SEDB: 💾 PHASE 5 — Bulk Persist · JDBC Batch Insert · 5K rows/batch
        loop For each gRPC chunk (5000 rows x 200 iterations)
            BE->>+SEDB: 7️⃣ JDBC executeBatch()<br/>5000 rows / batch<br/>@Transactional per chunk
            SEDB-->>-BE: 8️⃣ Batch ACK
        end
        Note right of BE: ✅ JDBC batch inserts chosen:<br/>• 200 round-trips vs 1M individual INSERTs<br/>• Spring JdbcTemplate.batchUpdate()<br/>• Transaction per chunk = bounded rollback scope<br/>• TimescaleDB hypertable for time-series partitioning
        deactivate BE
    end

    %% ============================================================================
    %% PHASE 6 — SE BACKEND → SE FRONTEND  (SSE progress events)
    %% ============================================================================

    rect rgb(224, 242, 254)
        Note over FE,BE: 📡 PHASE 6 — Progress and Completion · Server-Sent Events SSE
        BE-->>FE: 9️⃣ SSE text/event-stream<br/>event: progress pct 0   rows_done 0<br/>event: progress pct 45  rows_done 450000<br/>event: progress pct 100 rows_done 1000000
        Note right of BE: ✅ SSE for progress push:<br/>• Unidirectional server to client<br/>• Auto-reconnect via EventSource API<br/>• No polling — pure push<br/>• Tiny JSON events ~100 B each
        BE-->>-FE: 🔟 SSE event done<br/>job_id rows_persisted 1000000 duration_ms
        FE-->>User: ✅ 1 000 000 rows persisted successfully
    end

    %% ============================================================================
    %% PHASE 7 — USER EXPORTS RESULTS  (HTTP Chunked streaming, NDJSON or Parquet)
    %% ============================================================================

    rect rgb(254, 249, 195)
        Note over User,SEDB: 🔍 PHASE 7 — Optional Export · HTTP Chunked Transfer-Encoding
        User->>+FE: 1️⃣1️⃣ Request results export
        FE->>+BE: 1️⃣2️⃣ GET /api/smeagols/id/export<br/>Accept: application/x-ndjson<br/>OR Accept: application/octet-stream Parquet
        BE->>+SEDB: 1️⃣3️⃣ JDBC streaming SELECT server-side cursor
        SEDB-->>BE: 1️⃣4️⃣ Cursor row stream
        BE-->>-FE: 1️⃣5️⃣ HTTP Transfer-Encoding chunked<br/>Content-Type: application/x-ndjson<br/>OR Content-Disposition: attachment filename=result.parquet
        Note right of BE: ✅ HTTP Chunked Streaming:<br/>• Spring StreamingResponseBody<br/>• Never buffers 1M rows in JVM heap<br/>• NDJSON for browser / curl / Postman<br/>• Parquet for analytics (5-20x smaller than JSON)<br/>• Mid-stream errors via HTTP trailer headers
        FE-->>-User: 📊 Stream rendered or file downloaded
    end
